			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Eliminate IPC re-exports and migrate to legacy server\n\nRemove all `pub use` re-exports from `Source/IPC/mod.rs` to enforce explicit `Struct::Struct` import paths, aligning with the project's strict naming convention and recent entry-point refactoring. Callers must now reference the full nested path (e.g., `IPC::Connection::Manager::ConnectionManager`).\n\nSimultaneously, redirect IPC server instance references in `ConfigurationBridge.rs` and `StatusReporter.rs` from `TauriIPCServer` to `TauriIPCServer_Old`. This ensures compatibility with the current legacy server instance while the new implementation stabilizes. Add documentation to `AdvancedFeatures` noting the plan to atomize the 648-LOC single file into a directory.\n\nThis change reduces module resolution ambiguity and maintains IPC continuity during the ongoing architecture migration.",
			"SHA": "c85b6b3f4fceb80e8171ca8abe9de66da6baf67b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:37:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1128,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Extract Air DTOs into separate PascalCase modules\n\nRemove inline response and stream types from `AirClient.rs` and `AirServiceProvider.rs`, moving them into dedicated sibling modules (`AirMetrics`, `AirStatus`, `DownloadStream`, etc.) to enforce the project's strict `Struct::Struct` naming convention.\n\nUpdate all return types and struct instantiations to use the fully qualified paths (e.g., `UpdateInfo::Struct`, `FileInfo::Struct`). Additionally, migrate the `generate_request_id` helper function to a new `GenerateRequestID` module to align with the explicit `Fn` call path policy documented in recent refactoring commits.\n\nThis structural change eliminates the legacy stub file `AirServiceTypesStub.rs` by consolidating its contents into specific module files, reducing file density and ensuring consistency across the IPC layer.",
			"SHA": "85e894f4798397c9295b63c5a037829e310b89e0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T06:37:14Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1128,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Eliminate binary module re-exports for explicit paths\n\nRemove all `pub use` re-exports from `Source/Binary/mod.rs`, including those for `Main`, `Build`, `Register`, `Service`, and `Initialize`. Replace the legacy import shortcuts with a comment directing developers to use the full reverse-hierarchical path (`Binary::Main::Entry::Fn`, `Binary::Build::LocalhostPlugin::Fn`, etc.).\n\nThis aligns the entry point with the project's strict `Struct::Struct` naming convention and the `Nameless Exports` policy documented in `.claude/Naming-Convention.md`. The change enforces explicit call paths, reducing module resolution ambiguity and preventing reliance on convenience exports during the ongoing architecture migration.",
			"SHA": "83278ec9e89b6661773208e5146d7bd03e109e4b"
		}
